      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i've been seeing a lot about box breathing lately for stress. can u explain how it actually works on the body? like why does the specific timing of inhaling and holding breath help with anxiety?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing calms your nervous system by signaling your body to switch from a \"fight or flight\" state to a \"rest and digest\" mode. This rhythmic pattern slows your heart rate and triggers the release of calming neurotransmitters like GABA, while reducing the hormone cortisol that fuels anxiety. By maintaining a steady rhythm for both inhaling, holding, exhaling, and holding again, you create a powerful sensory anchor that directly interrupts the cycle of racing thoughts.",
